xref:lookup[Lookup of ``K~query~`` in ``pair<K, V>^{asterisk}^``]

. If ``pair<K, V>^{asterisk}^`` matches pattern ``[]``:
 .. Return ``·``.
. Else if let ``K~h~ → V~h~ {two-colons} ( K~t~ → V~t~ )^{asterisk}^`` be ``pair<K, V>^{asterisk}^``:
 .. Check that ``K~h~`` is equal to ``K~query~``.

 .. Return ``V~h~``.

. Otherwise:
 .. Otherwise:
  ... Check that ``pair<K, V>^{asterisk}^`` is a non-empty list.

  ... Let ``K~h~ → V~h~ {two-colons} ( K~t~ → V~t~ )^{asterisk}^`` be ``pair<K, V>^{asterisk}^``.
  ... Return xref:lookup[lookup of ``K~query~`` in ``( K~t~ → V~t~ )^{asterisk}^``].

xref:Check_expr[Check_expr]:

* Typechecking ``expr`` under context ``tenv``.

. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... If let ``literal`` be ``expr``:
   .... If let ``i`` be ``literal``:
    ..... Result in ``+INT+``.
   .... Else if let ``b`` be ``literal``:
    ..... Result in ``+BOOL+``.
  ... Else if let ``x`` be ``expr``:
   .... Let ``t`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:lookup[lookup of ``x`` in ``tenv``].
   .... Result in ``t``.
 .. {empty}
  ... If let ``+!+ e`` be ``expr``:
   .... Let ``type`` be the result of xref:Check_expr[typechecking ``e`` under context ``tenv``].
   .... Check that ``type`` matches pattern ``+BOOL+``.

   .... Result in ``+BOOL+``.
  ... Else if let ``e~l~ +++ e~r~`` be ``expr``:
   .... Let ``type`` be the result of xref:Check_expr[typechecking ``e~l~`` under context ``tenv``].
   .... Check that ``type`` matches pattern ``+INT+``.

   .... Let ``type'`` be the result of xref:Check_expr[typechecking ``e~r~`` under context ``tenv``].
   .... Check that ``type'`` matches pattern ``+INT+``.

   .... Result in ``+INT+``.
  ... Else if let ``e~l~ +<=+ e~r~`` be ``expr``:
   .... Let ``type`` be the result of xref:Check_expr[typechecking ``e~l~`` under context ``tenv``].
   .... Check that ``type`` matches pattern ``+INT+``.

   .... Let ``type'`` be the result of xref:Check_expr[typechecking ``e~r~`` under context ``tenv``].
   .... Check that ``type'`` matches pattern ``+INT+``.

   .... Result in ``+BOOL+``.
  ... Else if let ``e~l~ +&&+ e~r~`` be ``expr``:
   .... Let ``type`` be the result of xref:Check_expr[typechecking ``e~l~`` under context ``tenv``].
   .... Check that ``type`` matches pattern ``+BOOL+``.

   .... Let ``type'`` be the result of xref:Check_expr[typechecking ``e~r~`` under context ``tenv``].
   .... Check that ``type'`` matches pattern ``+BOOL+``.

   .... Result in ``+BOOL+``.

xref:Check_command[Check_command]:

* Typechecking ``command`` under context ``tenv``.

. If ``command`` matches pattern ``+SKIP+``:
 .. Result in ``tenv``.
. Else if let ``t x +=+ e`` be ``command``:
 .. Let ``type`` be the result of xref:Check_expr[typechecking ``e`` under context ``tenv``].
 .. Check that ``type`` is equal to ``t``.

 .. Result in ``x → t {two-colons} tenv``.
. Else if let ``x +=+ e`` be ``command``:
 .. Let ``t`` be the result of xref:Check_expr[typechecking ``e`` under context ``tenv``].
 .. Check that xref:lookup[lookup of ``x`` in ``tenv``] is equal to ``t``.

 .. Result in ``tenv``.
. Else if let ``+IF+ e +THEN+ c~1~ +ELSE+ c~2~ +END+`` be ``command``:
 .. Let ``type`` be the result of xref:Check_expr[typechecking ``e`` under context ``tenv``].
 .. Check that ``type`` matches pattern ``+BOOL+``.

 .. Let ``tenv~1~`` be the result of xref:Check_command[typechecking ``c~1~`` under context ``tenv``].
 .. Let ``tenv~2~`` be the result of xref:Check_command[typechecking ``c~2~`` under context ``tenv``].
 .. Result in ``tenv``.
. Else if let ``+WHILE+ e +DO+ c +END+`` be ``command``:
 .. Let ``type`` be the result of xref:Check_expr[typechecking ``e`` under context ``tenv``].
 .. Check that ``type`` matches pattern ``+BOOL+``.

 .. Let ``tenv~1~`` be the result of xref:Check_command[typechecking ``c`` under context ``tenv``].
 .. Result in ``tenv``.
. Else if let ``c~1~ +;+ c~2~`` be ``command``:
 .. Let ``tenv~1~`` be the result of xref:Check_command[typechecking ``c~1~`` under context ``tenv``].
 .. Let ``tenv~2~`` be the result of xref:Check_command[typechecking ``c~2~`` under context ``tenv~1~``].
 .. Result in ``tenv~2~``.

xref:Check_prog[Check_prog]:

* Program ``command`` is well-typed

. Let ``tenv`` be the result of xref:Check_command[typechecking ``command`` under context ``·``].
. The relation holds.

xref:Eval_expr[Eval_expr]:

* Evaluating ``expr`` in environment ``env``.

. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... If let ``literal`` be ``expr``:
   .... If let ``i`` be ``literal``:
    ..... Result in xref:literal[the integer ``i``].
   .... Else if let ``b`` be ``literal``:
    ..... Result in xref:literal[the boolean ``b``].
  ... Else if let ``x`` be ``expr``:
   .... Let ``v`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:lookup[lookup of ``x`` in ``env``].
   .... Result in ``v``.
 .. {empty}
  ... If let ``+!+ e`` be ``expr``:
   .... Let ``literal`` be the result of xref:Eval_expr[evaluating ``e`` in environment ``env``].
   .... Let!~type~ ``b~e~`` be ``literal``.

   .... Let ``b`` be not ``b~e~``.
   .... Result in xref:literal[the boolean ``b``].
  ... Else if let ``e~l~ +++ e~r~`` be ``expr``:
   .... Let ``literal`` be the result of xref:Eval_expr[evaluating ``e~l~`` in environment ``env``].
   .... Let!~type~ ``i~l~`` be ``literal``.

   .... Let ``literal'`` be the result of xref:Eval_expr[evaluating ``e~r~`` in environment ``env``].
   .... Let!~type~ ``i~r~`` be ``literal'``.

   .... Let ``i`` be ``i~l~`` + ``i~r~``.
   .... Result in xref:literal[the integer ``i``].
  ... Else if let ``e~l~ +<=+ e~r~`` be ``expr``:
   .... Let ``literal`` be the result of xref:Eval_expr[evaluating ``e~l~`` in environment ``env``].
   .... Let!~type~ ``i~l~`` be ``literal``.

   .... Let ``literal'`` be the result of xref:Eval_expr[evaluating ``e~r~`` in environment ``env``].
   .... Let!~type~ ``i~r~`` be ``literal'``.

   .... Let ``b`` be ``i~l~`` is less than or equal to ``i~r~``.
   .... Result in xref:literal[the boolean ``b``].
  ... Else if let ``e~l~ +&&+ e~r~`` be ``expr``:
   .... Let ``literal`` be the result of xref:Eval_expr[evaluating ``e~l~`` in environment ``env``].
   .... Let!~type~ ``b~l~`` be ``literal``.

   .... Let ``literal'`` be the result of xref:Eval_expr[evaluating ``e~r~`` in environment ``env``].
   .... Let!~type~ ``b~r~`` be ``literal'``.

   .... Let ``b`` be ``b~l~`` and ``b~r~``.
   .... Result in xref:literal[the boolean ``b``].

xref:Eval_command[Eval_command]:

* Executing ``command`` in environment ``env``.

. If ``command`` matches pattern ``+SKIP+``:
 .. Result in ``env``.
. Else if let ``t x +=+ e`` be ``command``:
 .. Let ``v`` be the result of xref:Eval_expr[evaluating ``e`` in environment ``env``].
 .. Result in ``x → v {two-colons} env``.
. Else if let ``x +=+ e`` be ``command``:
 .. Let ``v`` be the result of xref:Eval_expr[evaluating ``e`` in environment ``env``].
 .. Result in ``x → v {two-colons} env``.
. Else if let ``+IF+ e +THEN+ c~1~ +ELSE+ c~2~ +END+`` be ``command``:
 .. Let ``literal`` be the result of xref:Eval_expr[evaluating ``e`` in environment ``env``].
 .. Try:
  ... {empty}
   .... Check that ``literal`` is equal to xref:literal[the boolean ``true``].

   .... Let ``env~1~`` be the result of xref:Eval_command[executing ``c~1~`` in environment ``env``].
   .... Result in ``env~1~``.
  ... {empty}
   .... Check that ``literal`` is equal to xref:literal[the boolean ``false``].

   .... Let ``env~2~`` be the result of xref:Eval_command[executing ``c~2~`` in environment ``env``].
   .... Result in ``env~2~``.
. Else if let ``+WHILE+ e +DO+ c +END+`` be ``command``:
 .. Let ``literal`` be the result of xref:Eval_expr[evaluating ``e`` in environment ``env``].
 .. Try:
  ... {empty}
   .... Check that ``literal`` is equal to xref:literal[the boolean ``false``].

   .... Result in ``env``.
  ... {empty}
   .... Check that ``literal`` is equal to xref:literal[the boolean ``true``].

   .... Let ``env~1~`` be the result of xref:Eval_command[executing ``c`` in environment ``env``].
   .... Let ``env~2~`` be the result of xref:Eval_command[executing ``+WHILE+ e +DO+ c +END+`` in environment ``env~1~``].
   .... Result in ``env~2~``.
. Else if let ``c~1~ +;+ c~2~`` be ``command``:
 .. Let ``env~1~`` be the result of xref:Eval_command[executing ``c~1~`` in environment ``env``].
 .. Let ``env~2~`` be the result of xref:Eval_command[executing ``c~2~`` in environment ``env~1~``].
 .. Result in ``env~2~``.

xref:Eval_prog[Eval_prog]:

* Executing program ``command``.

. Let ``env`` be the result of xref:Eval_command[executing ``command`` in environment ``·``].
. Result in ``env``.

xref:Run_prog[Run_prog]:

* Running program ``command``.

. If xref:Check_prog[program ``command`` is well-typed]:
 .. Let ``env`` be the result of xref:Eval_prog[executing program ``command``].
 .. Result in ``env``.
